## AI-Assisted

## Instance-parent directory for the pam_namespace 'user'-method polydir
## /var/tmp (/etc/security/namespace.d/30_security-misc.conf).
##
## pam_namespace requires the instance_prefix parent to pre-exist, owned
## root:root, mode 0000 (the restrictive mode is the isolation guarantee; a
## laxer mode would let one account reach another's instance). Shipping it via
## tmpfiles.d (not postinst) makes it self-healing: recreated at every boot
## with the enforced mode, surviving reboots and systemd-tmpfiles age cleanup.
## Age argument '-' means never auto-clean the per-account instances inside.
##
## The /tmp and /dev/shm lines use the 'tmpfs' method, which mounts a fresh
## empty filesystem and does NOT use an instance-parent dir (verified), so
## none is created for them.
##
## man tmpfiles.d
d /var/tmp/tmp-inst  0000 root root -
